{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via system/task instructions, no interactive back-and-forth messages from a human user occurred in this conversation — it was a single autonomous task) asked me to: \"Build the cinema seat-booking web application described in spec/README.md, as the Angular application already set up in this Nx workspace (Nx project `cinescope` in apps/cinescope); its stack is described in spec/stack.md. The work is split into tickets in spec/tickets/; implement them in order. spec/README.md is the complete specification: do not ask any questions, and where it is silent choose the simplest option that satisfies it. Finish only when every ticket is done and `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds.\"\n   \n   No human user sent any follow-up messages during this session — all turns after the initial task were my own tool-call results and one mandatory system instruction to produce this summary without tool calls. There is no explicit user feedback to incorporate beyond the original task description.\n\n   Security/constraint instructions from the spec that must be preserved verbatim in intent:\n   - \"The package manager is pnpm. Do not use `npm` or `yarn`.\"\n   - \"The application is served at `http://localhost:4200`. Do not change the port.\"\n   - \"Do not add dependencies. Everything the application needs is already installed.\"\n   - \"Do not edit `db.json` by hand. It is the backend's data.\"\n   - \"The application is desktop-only (viewport 1280 × 720 or larger). All user-facing text is in English.\"\n   - \"Do not change the date logic to see screenings\" (even though today's real date has no matching screenings in db.json, this is expected and must not be worked around in the app).\n   - Section 9: `data-testid` names/values are a strict contract — \"do not rename, abbreviate or prefix them, and do not put these `data-testid` values on any other element.\"\n   - Section 11 \"Out of scope\": do not build user accounts, real payment processing, seat locking between concurrent customers, updating `occupiedSeats` after a reservation, posters/images, mobile/responsive layouts, keyboard navigation/ARIA beyond browser/UI-library defaults, or translations.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Nx 23 monorepo, Angular 22 standalone zoneless app, Angular Router, SCSS, Vitest, ESLint.\n   - Angular Material 22 + CDK (no `@angular/animations` package installed — confirmed Material 22 handles this gracefully via internal `_animationsDisabled()` detection, so `provideAnimationsAsync()`/`BrowserAnimationsModule` must NOT be added).\n   - Angular Signals (`signal`, `computed`, `effect`) as the primary reactive state mechanism (required since app is zoneless).\n   - `toSignal` from `@angular/core/rxjs-interop` to bridge `ActivatedRoute.queryParamMap` into a signal.\n   - Reactive Forms (`ReactiveFormsModule`, `FormBuilder.nonNullable.group`, custom sync validators).\n   - `sessionStorage`-backed booking state service (survives reload, cleared on Cancel/Continue-from-confirmation).\n   - Functional Router guards (`CanActivateFn`) for booking-state-gated routes.\n   - `MatSnackBar.openFromComponent` for toast notifications (single-at-a-time, 4s duration, custom `data-testid=\"toast\"` content component).\n   - `json-server` 0.17.4 backend (`GET /movies`, `GET /screenings`, `GET /screenings?date=`, `GET /screenings/:id`, `POST /reservations`), base URL `http://localhost:3000`.\n   - Chrome DevTools Protocol (CDP) driven directly via Node's built-in `fetch`/`WebSocket` (no Playwright/Puppeteer installed) for end-to-end browser testing, using a Playwright-downloaded Chrome binary at `/opt/ms-playwright/chromium-1234/chrome-linux/chrome`.\n   - Pure-function modules for domain logic: `auditorium.ts` (seat-map geometry/state), `seat-utils.ts` (seat id parsing, pricing, selection grouping/ordering), `date-utils.ts` (ISO date parsing/formatting, weekday/month names, \"show date\" format).\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   - **`spec/README.md`, `spec/stack.md`, `spec/tickets/*.md`** — read in full; these are the complete, authoritative specification driving every decision. Not modified.\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/core/models.ts`** (created) — Domain types:\n     ```ts\n     export interface Movie { id: number; title: string; genre: string; runtimeMinutes: number; format: 'PL dubbing' | 'PL subtitles'; }\n     export interface Screening { id: number; movieId: number; date: string; time: string; occupiedSeats: string[]; }\n     export interface ReservationCustomer { firstName: string; lastName: string; email: string; phone: string; }\n     export interface Reservation { id: number; screeningId: number; seats: string[]; customer: ReservationCustomer; totalPrice: number; }\n     export interface ReservationRequest { screeningId: number; seats: string[]; customer: ReservationCustomer; totalPrice: number; }\n     ```\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/core/seat-utils.ts`** (created, then edited once for lint) — `MAX_SEATS=10`, `COUCH_ROW=15`, `seatId(row,column)`→`R{row}C{column}`, `parseSeatId(id)`, `rowPrice(row)` (≤5→25, ≤10→32, ≤14→39, else→89), `formatPrice(amount)`→`\"{n.toFixed(2)} PLN\"`, `SelectionUnit` interface `{row, columnStart, columnEnd?, ids, isCouch, price}`, `buildUnits(seats)` (groups flat seat-id array into ordered seat/couch units by row then column — final fixed version iterates `[...byRow.entries()].sort(([a],[b])=>a-b)` to avoid non-null assertions), `groupSelectionByRow(seats)` (returns `{row,label}[]` for the selected-seats panel, e.g. `Row 15: 1-2`), `orderedSeatIds(seats)` (flattened unit ids in summary order, for the reservation POST), `totalPrice(seats)`.\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/core/auditorium.ts`** (created) — `CellState = 'available'|'selected'|'unavailable'|'accessible'`; `SeatCellView`, `CouchCellView`, `GapCellView` (`'entrance'|'aisle'`), `CellView` union, `RowView{row,cells}`. `ACCESSIBLE_COLUMNS = new Set([10,11,12,13,14,15])`. `buildAuditorium(occupied, selected)` builds all 15 rows: rows ≥11 get a left block (cols 1-4, or 2 couches for row 15), rows <11 get `{kind:'entrance'}`; then `{kind:'aisle'}`; then middle block cols 5-20 (or 8 couches for row 15, step 2); then `{kind:'aisle'}`; then right block cols 21-24 (or 2 couches for row 15). Row 1 columns 10-15 marked `'accessible'` when free. Couch state checks both its two seat ids for selected/occupied.\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/core/date-utils.ts`** (created) — `startOfDay`, `addDays`, `isoDate(date)`→`YYYY-MM-DD`, `parseIsoDate(value)` (strict round-trip validation), `weekdayName(date)` (full English names array), `showDate(isoDateValue, time)`→`\"<Weekday> <D> <Mon> <HH:mm>\"` e.g. `\"Tuesday 15 Sep 16:00\"`, `resolveSelectedDate(param)` — implements \"missing, invalid, or past date → today\" rule using `startOfDay(new Date())` as baseline.\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/core/api.service.ts`** (created) — `ApiService` with `BASE_URL='http://localhost:3000'`; `getMovies()`, `getScreeningsByDate(date)` (uses `HttpParams`), `getScreening(id)`, `createReservation(request)` (POST).\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/core/booking.service.ts`** (created) — `CheckoutFormValues{firstName,lastName,email,confirmEmail,phone,termsAccepted}`; `BookingState{screeningId,seats,form,paid,email}`; `STORAGE_KEY='cinescope-booking'`; signal-backed with `load()`/`persist()` to/from `sessionStorage`. Public API: `booking` (readonly signal), `ensureBookingFor(screeningId)` (keeps existing unpaid booking for same screening id, else creates fresh empty one), `belongsToUnpaid(screeningId)`, `isPaid()`, `setSeats(seats)`, `updateForm(partial)`, `markPaid(email)`, `clear()`.\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/core/toast.component.ts`** (created, then fixed for lint) — Final version:\n     ```ts\n     import { Component, inject } from '@angular/core';\n     import { MAT_SNACK_BAR_DATA } from '@angular/material/snack-bar';\n\n     @Component({\n       selector: 'app-toast',\n       template: `<span data-testid=\"toast\">{{ message }}</span>`,\n     })\n     export class ToastComponent {\n       private readonly data = inject<{ message: string }>(MAT_SNACK_BAR_DATA);\n       readonly message = this.data.message;\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/core/toast.service.ts`** (created) — `ToastService.show(message)` calls `snackBar.openFromComponent(ToastComponent, {data:{message}, duration:4000})`.\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/core/guards.ts`** (created) — `inProgressBookingGuard`: valid only if booking exists, matches route's `:id` param as `screeningId`, is unpaid, and has ≥1 seat — else redirects to `/`. `paidBookingGuard`: valid only if `bookingService.isPaid()` — else redirects to `/`.\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/app.config.ts`** (edited) — Final:\n     ```ts\n     import { ApplicationConfig, provideBrowserGlobalErrorListeners } from '@angular/core';\n     import { provideHttpClient } from '@angular/common/http';\n     import { provideNativeDateAdapter } from '@angular/material/core';\n     import { provideRouter } from '@angular/router';\n     import { appRoutes } from './app.routes';\n\n     export const appConfig: ApplicationConfig = {\n       providers: [\n         provideBrowserGlobalErrorListeners(),\n         provideRouter(appRoutes),\n         provideNativeDateAdapter(),\n         provideHttpClient(),\n       ],\n     };\n     ```\n     (Deliberately does NOT include animations providers — `@angular/animations` package is not installed in this workspace, and Material 22 works without it.)\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/app.routes.ts`** (edited) — final content shown in full above in the Errors/analysis section; registers all 5 routes + wildcard redirect, with guards on summary/checkout/confirmation.\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/features/movie-list/{movie-list.ts,.html,.scss}`** (created) — `MovieListComponent`: day picker (`day-picker`/`day-button`×5 with `data-date`/`data-selected`, plus `mat-datepicker` wrapped in `mat-form-field` with `data-testid=\"date-picker\"`, `[min]=\"minDate\"`), movie list with loading/error/empty states (`movies-loading`, `movies-error`+`movies-retry-button`, `movies-empty`), `movie-card` with `movie-title`/`movie-genre`/`movie-runtime`/`movie-format` and `screening-button`×N (`data-screening-id`). Uses `effect(() => this.load(this.selectedDateIso()))` in the constructor to both perform the initial load and reload whenever the resolved date changes; `forkJoin({movies, screenings})` for fetching.\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/features/seat-map/{seat-map.ts,.html,.scss}`** (created) — `SeatMapComponent`: loads screening via `api.getScreening(id)`, then `api.getMovies()` to find the matching movie (sequential, nested subscribe — NOT forkJoin, since forkJoin would need the movie id first); on any failure navigates to `/`; on success calls `bookingService.ensureBookingFor(screeningId)`. Renders title/subtitle/seat-limit-info/screen-indicator/seat-map (via `buildAuditorium` computed from occupied+selected sets)/legend/selected-seats panel/cancel+continue buttons. `toggleSeat`/`toggleCouch` enforce the 10-seat cap and call `toast.show('Maximum 10 seats per booking')` when exceeded.\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/features/summary/{summary.ts,.html,.scss}`** (created) — `SummaryComponent`: loads screening+movie (redirect to `/` on failure), builds `rows` via `buildUnits(seats)` mapped to display rows with `title`/`datetime`/`seatDescription`/`priceText`; `remove(unit)` filters out the unit's ids and navigates to the seat map if the booking becomes empty; `back()`/`confirm()` navigation; `summary-total` renders `\"Total: {{ totalText() }}\"`.\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/features/checkout/{checkout.ts,.html,.scss}`** (created) — `CheckoutComponent`: custom validators `emailFormatValidator` (regex `/^[^\\s@]+@[^\\s@]+\\.[^\\s@]+$/`), `phoneFormatValidator` (regex `/^\\d{9}$/`, skipped when empty), `confirmEmailMatchValidator` (compares `control.parent.get('email').value`). `fb.nonNullable.group(...)` with `Validators.required`/`minLength(2)`/`requiredTrue` as applicable. Restores saved form values from `bookingService.booking()?.form` via `patchValue(saved, {emitEvent:false})` without marking touched. `form.valueChanges.subscribe(value => bookingService.updateForm(value))`. `email.valueChanges` triggers `confirmEmail.updateValueAndValidity({emitEvent:false})`. `fieldError(name,label,ruleMessage)` helper (shows `\"{label} is required\"` if `required` error and touched, else rule message if invalid and touched, else null). Separate `confirmEmailError`/`termsError` getters. `markTermsTouched()` bound to checkbox `(change)` event (per spec: toggling, not blurring, marks it \"left\"). `pay()`: if invalid → `markAllAsTouched()` + toast `'The form contains errors'`, no request; if valid → POST reservation with `orderedSeatIds(booking.seats)`, `totalPrice(booking.seats)`, customer fields (`phone: value.phone || ''`); on success → `bookingService.markPaid(value.email)` + navigate to `/confirmation`; on error → toast `'Payment failed. Please try again.'`. `payLabel` computed signal: `submitting() ? 'Processing…' : 'Pay ' + totalText`.\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/features/confirmation/{confirmation.ts,.html,.scss}`** (created) — simple: reads `bookingService.booking()?.email`, `continue()` clears booking and navigates to `/`.\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/app.spec.ts`** (pre-existing, NOT yet reviewed/fixed) — currently just does `TestBed.configureTestingModule({imports:[App]})` then asserts the component instance is truthy. This has NOT been verified to still pass now that `App`'s template renders a real `<router-outlet>` wired to routes requiring `HttpClient`/Material/etc. providers — flagged as unverified, pending `pnpm nx test cinescope` run.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Broken async code in draft `movie-list.ts`**: caught before running; rewrote cleanly using top-level `effect()` from `@angular/core` instead of invalid `await import(...)` inside a field initializer.\n   - **Dead/wrong code in draft `seat-map.ts`**: a stray `forkJoin({screening: api.getScreening(id), movie: api.getScreening(id)})` (duplicate, wrong) was present as unused dead code; removed via `Edit`, then removed the now-unused `forkJoin` import via a second `Edit`.\n   - **`pnpm nx build cinescope` initial failure**: `[ERR_PNPM_ABORTED_REMOVE_MODULES_DIR_NO_TTY]` — Nx tried to auto-run `pnpm install` (removing/recreating `node_modules`) without a TTY present. Fixed by running with `CI=true` prefix: `CI=true pnpm nx build cinescope`. After this, build succeeded (dependencies got reinstalled/recreated fully, matching original versions) — Angular bundle: `main-IIGMKEWL.js 686.17 kB`, `styles 7.96 kB`, total 694.13 kB, with a non-fatal WARNING that the initial bundle (694.13 kB) exceeds the 500 kB budget by 194.13 kB. This is a warning only; the build command still exits successfully, satisfying \"`pnpm nx build cinescope` must succeed.\"\n   - **`pnpm nx lint cinescope` found 2 problems**:\n     1. `toast.component.ts:11:43` — error `@angular-eslint/prefer-inject` (constructor-param `@Inject(...)` injection) — fixed by switching to `inject()` field initializer.\n     2. `seat-utils.ts:49:25` — warning `@typescript-eslint/no-non-null-assertion` (`byRow.get(row)!`) — fixed by restructuring to iterate `byRow.entries()` directly, avoiding the non-null assertion.\n     After both fixes: `✔ All files pass linting`, and rebuild re-confirmed success (694.12 kB, same non-fatal budget warning).\n   - **Orphaned background `json-server` processes causing `EADDRINUSE`**: An initial test command `(cd /workspace/project && (pnpm api > /tmp/api.log 2>&1 &) && sleep 2 && curl ...)` failed because `curl` isn't installed in this environment, but the backgrounded `pnpm api`/`json-server` subprocess (started via plain `&`, NOT via the Bash tool's `run_in_background` tracking) kept running as an orphan (PIDs 882 `sh -c json-server...` and 883 `node .../json-server/lib/cli/bin.js ...`). Later legitimate attempts to start `pnpm api` via `run_in_background: true` failed repeatedly with `EADDRINUSE: address already in use ::1:3000` because of these orphans. Diagnosed by iterating `/proc/[0-9]*/cmdline` (since `ps` is unavailable in this minimal container) and found/killed them with `kill -9 882 883`. After that, `pnpm api` started cleanly under new background task id `bjn2r6lv4`.\n   - **Raw Node `fetch()` to `http://localhost:3000` failing with ECONNREFUSED despite the server being up**: Diagnosed as a quirk of `json-server`'s default `--host localhost` binding (which in this sandbox binds only to `::1`, confirmed via `--help` output showing `-H, --host  Set host [default: \"localhost\"]` and via the `EADDRINUSE ... ::1:3000` error text), combined with Node's `fetch`/undici picking the IPv4 address (`127.0.0.1`) despite `dns.lookup(..., {all:true})` returning `::1` first — an inconsistency specific to raw Node `fetch`, confirmed NOT to be a real app/environment problem because `http://[::1]:3000/movies` fetched fine directly, and — most importantly — the actual headless-Chrome-driven end-to-end test later succeeded completely against `http://localhost:3000` with zero failed network requests. No code change was made to work around this (correctly, since it wasn't a real defect); I explicitly decided NOT to modify the `pnpm api` script in `package.json` (e.g., adding `--host 0.0.0.0`) since it wasn't necessary and wasn't part of the ticket scope.\n   - **No browser-automation tooling pre-installed** (`chromium-cli` not found, no `playwright` npm package, no project `.claude/skills/*/SKILL.md` for running this app)