{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CgDCY4BH5U2fhWFPdcXFo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`db.json` is clean again, and everything else reflects the actual implementation (`.pnpm-store/` is pnpm's local package cache, not part of the deliverable — safe to ignore).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe cinema seat-booking app is complete and verified end-to-end against the full spec:\n\n- **Guards**: direct navigation to `/screenings/:id/summary`, `/screenings/:id/checkout`, or `/confirmation` without a valid booking correctly redirects to `/`.\n- **Seat map**: 10-seat cap enforced with the exact toast `Maximum 10 seats per booking`; Cancel clears the booking and returns home; all geometry/testids (`aisle`×30, `row-label-left`/`row-label-right`×15 each, `seat-map`, `cancel-button`) are present and correct.\n- **Summary**: removing the last item redirects back to the seat map; Back preserves the seat selection.\n- **Checkout**: empty-field, invalid-email, mismatched-confirm-email, invalid-phone, and unchecked-terms validation messages all match the spec's exact wording; invalid submit shows toast `The form contains errors` without navigating; Back preserves typed values, and re-entering the form retains them.\n- Unit tests (`pnpm nx test cinescope`) and `pnpm nx build cinescope` both still pass (build succeeds with only the pre-existing non-fatal bundle-size budget warning).\n- Cleaned up the leftover headless-Chrome test process and reverted `db.json` to its original committed state (it had picked up a test reservation and reformatting from my CDP-driven testing).\n\nAll tickets in `spec/tickets/` are implemented and the acceptance criteria in `spec/README.md` section 10 have been walked through and confirmed. The dev server (`bylxqmgv1`) and API (`bjn2r6lv4`) background tasks are still running if you want to continue interacting with the app manually."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,